Page 17074 smeagan: <begin> {{ang-verb|smēaġan}}<ref>{{R:ang:GOE|volume=2|285|Thus, there were two stems within the OE paradigm, ''smēaġ-'' and ''smēa-'' [...] and in all dialects but Kt and the dialect of PsGl(A), the latter stem could be substituted for the former, leading to innovations like Bo 41.146.21 ''smēan'' pres.subj.pl., Li ''smēas'' pres.ind.pl., ''smēande'' pres.part. Only in Li ''smēaġe'', Ru2 ''smēoġe'' imper.sg. do we see replacement of the latter stem by the former, if these are not in fact infinitives.}}</ref> <end>
